<!--
  Ore data pack for OreRedistLinux. Packs are plain data: nothing in them is ever executed.
  Only files in this folder whose root element is <OreDataPack Format="1" Tool="OreRedistLinux"> are loaded.

  Ore Name     Ore name as in the planet definition. "Iron" matches Iron_02, Iron_01... ("Iron_02" matches only that one).
  Abundance    Optional. How common the ore is in the Earth's crust (ppm by mass). Used by "Set weights from rarity".
  Rocks        Optional. Five numbers 0-1000 separated by ; = suitability for
               Sedimentary ; Metamorphic low grade ; Metamorphic high grade ; Igneous extrusive ; Igneous intrusive.
               0 = never forms in this rock, 100 = normal, higher = prefers it. Used by the geology placement mode.
  Size         Optional. Size of a vein of this ore in pixels on the reference planet (EarthLike, 60 km radius; the tool scales it for other planet
               sizes). Real deposits differ a lot: tiny silver veins and impact minerals (4-10) up to huge reefs, sedimentary basins and oil fields (60-75).
               Built-in sizes: footprint of a typical deposit (km2) -> 15 x km2^0.35 pixels (1 km2 = 15, 100 km2 = 75), so the range is squeezed for the game.
  Glob         Optional. Regional strength 0-100: 0 = the ore is spread evenly, 100 = it only occurs in a few regions (like gold in greenstone belts,
               nickel at Sudbury). In geology mode the regions also lie where the ore's rocks are.
  GlobSize     Optional. Size of the regions in km (the planet default is 15). GlobCoverage: share of the planet in percent inside the regions (default 20).
               The built-in packs size the regions from real deposits: the diameter of a real district or belt (Bushveld 350 km, Witwatersrand 300 km,
               Athabasca 250 km...) x 0.047 (the 120 km planet is 1/106 of Earth, with an allowance of x5 for being a game), but at least about 8 km;
               the number of regions is how many such districts the planet gets. The coverage is that number times the area of a region (0.5 % = a few
               small regions, 7 % = a few big basins) and the size is the noise size that gives that number of regions (measured: 50 km / 1 % = 2 regions,
               32 km / 1 % = 4, 27 km / 1 % = 6, 20 km / 0.5 % = 5; bigger size = fewer regions). Regions are in km, so a smaller planet gets fewer.
  Order        Packs are applied in order (lowest first); a later pack overrides an ore of an earlier one.
-->
<OreDataPack Format="1" Tool="OreRedistLinux" Name="Vanilla" Author="OreRedistLinux" Order="0"
             Description="The nine vanilla ores and Ice: abundance in the Earth's crust and the rock types they form in.">
  <Ore Name="Silicon"   Abundance="282000" Rocks="80;60;50;40;70" Glob="0" Size="59" />  <!-- size: quartz sand and quartzite beds about 50 km2 -> 59 px -->
  <Ore Name="Iron"      Abundance="56300"  Rocks="80;60;50;15;40" Glob="40" GlobSize="37.5" GlobCoverage="6" Size="49" />  <!-- ~6 regions of about 24 km; real: Hamersley, Carajas, Superior banded iron basins, 500 km ; size: a banded iron deposit like Mt Whaleback about 30 km2 -> 49 px -->
  <Ore Name="Magnesium" Abundance="23300"  Rocks="100;60;40;10;30" Glob="20" GlobSize="32.5" GlobCoverage="2" Size="31" />  <!-- ~6 regions of about 14 km; real: magnesite and dolomite basins, 300 km ; size: magnesite deposits about 8 km2 -> 31 px -->
  <Ore Name="Nickel"    Abundance="84"     Rocks="10;10;30;60;100" Glob="75" GlobSize="20" GlobCoverage="0.5" Size="19" />  <!-- ~5 regions of about 8 km; real: Sudbury, Norilsk, Kambalda, 150 km ; size: a sulfide orebody like Sudbury mines about 2 km2 -> 19 px -->
  <Ore Name="Cobalt"    Abundance="25"     Rocks="50;40;30;30;70" Glob="70" GlobSize="32.5" GlobCoverage="0.5" Size="22" />  <!-- ~3 regions of about 10 km; real: Katanga copper-cobalt belt, Bou Azzer, 250 km ; size: a Katanga copper-cobalt deposit about 3 km2 -> 22 px -->
  <Ore Name="Uranium"   Abundance="2.7"    Rocks="80;30;30;20;60" Glob="70" GlobSize="32.5" GlobCoverage="1" Size="17" />  <!-- ~5 regions of about 11 km; real: Athabasca, Kazakhstan basins, Olympic Dam, 250 km ; size: a roll-front or unconformity deposit about 1.5 km2 -> 17 px -->
  <Ore Name="Uraninite"  Abundance="2.7"    Rocks="80;30;30;20;60" Glob="70" GlobSize="32.5" GlobCoverage="1" Size="17" />  <!-- ~5 regions of about 11 km; real: Athabasca, Kazakhstan basins, Olympic Dam, 250 km ; size: a roll-front or unconformity deposit about 1.5 km2 -> 17 px -->  <!-- the vanilla uranium ore is the voxel material Uraninite_01 -->
  <Ore Name="Silver"    Abundance="0.075"  Rocks="20;40;20;90;60" Glob="55" GlobSize="27.5" GlobCoverage="1" Size="10" />  <!-- ~6 regions of about 10 km; real: Mexican silver belt, Andes, Nevada, 200 km ; size: a silver vein system about 0.3 km2 -> 10 px -->
  <Ore Name="Platinum"  Abundance="0.005"  Rocks="5;5;20;20;100" Glob="90" GlobSize="50" GlobCoverage="1.5" Size="75" />  <!-- ~3 regions of about 17 km; real: Bushveld complex, Norilsk, 350 km ; size: a PGE reef like the Merensky Reef about 100 km2 -> 75 px -->
  <Ore Name="Gold"      Abundance="0.004"  Rocks="25;100;50;40;50" Glob="75" GlobSize="32.5" GlobCoverage="2" Size="15" />  <!-- ~6 regions of about 14 km; real: Witwatersrand, Yilgarn, Abitibi, 300 km ; size: an orogenic gold deposit about 1 km2 -> 15 px -->
  <!-- Ice is not a crust ore: no abundance, no rock preference -->
  <Ore Name="Ice" Rocks="100;100;100;100;100" Glob="0" />
</OreDataPack>
